<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Docs on Totally</title><link>https://totally.sh/docs/</link><description>Recent content in Docs on Totally</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="https://totally.sh/docs/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Files and discovery</title><link>https://totally.sh/docs/files/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://totally.sh/docs/files/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;files&lt;/code&gt; is a diagnostic command for the raw local transcripts Totally finds.
Use &lt;a href="sessions/"&gt;Sessions&lt;/a&gt; for normal browsing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally files
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally files --archived
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally files --latest
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Use focused output when diagnosing storage or discovery:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally files --paths
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally files --count
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally files --summary
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally files --limit &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;20&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;files verify&lt;/code&gt; parses transcript files and reports malformed records and
impossible token counters. With no paths, it verifies all discovered files.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally files verify
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally files verify ~/.codex/sessions/.../rollout-*.jsonl
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally files verify --format json
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The command exits with a non-zero status when it finds an issue. It accepts
&lt;code&gt;.jsonl&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;.jsonl.zst&lt;/code&gt; transcript paths.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Getting started</title><link>https://totally.sh/docs/getting-started/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://totally.sh/docs/getting-started/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Install Totally with the shell installer:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;curl -fsSL https://totally.sh/install.sh | sh
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The installer places the executable in &lt;code&gt;~/.local/bin&lt;/code&gt; by default. Set
&lt;code&gt;TOTALLY_INSTALL_DIR&lt;/code&gt; to choose another directory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have Go installed, you can also install the latest version directly:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;go install github.com/rybkr/totally/cmd/totally@latest
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Run a first usage report:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally stats --since 7d
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Then list the sessions Totally found:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally sessions
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Totally discovers supported local agent homes automatically. Use &lt;code&gt;--home&lt;/code&gt; when
you want to inspect a specific location or combine more than one location.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Global options</title><link>https://totally.sh/docs/global-options/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://totally.sh/docs/global-options/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;These options apply to Totally commands unless a command&amp;rsquo;s help text says
otherwise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-text" data-lang="text"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;--agent AGENT Session format to discover: all or codex
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;--home PATH Agent home directory; may be repeated
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;--config PATH Configuration file path
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;--archived Include archived sessions
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;--since TIME, --after TIME Include sessions at or after TIME
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;--until TIME, --before TIME Include sessions at or before TIME
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;--format table|json Select output format
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;--no-pager Disable terminal paging
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Time values accept relative durations such as &lt;code&gt;7d&lt;/code&gt;, calendar dates such as
&lt;code&gt;2026-07-01&lt;/code&gt;, RFC3339 timestamps, and the words &lt;code&gt;today&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;yesterday&lt;/code&gt;, and
&lt;code&gt;now&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Pricing</title><link>https://totally.sh/docs/pricing/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://totally.sh/docs/pricing/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Totally estimates cost from a bundled local pricing catalog. It is useful for
understanding usage, not for reconciling a vendor invoice.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally prices
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally prices --model gpt-5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally prices --provider openai --format json
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Price rows include input, cached-input, and output rates per million tokens,
along with their source and effective date.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can overlay a bundled rate in Totally&amp;rsquo;s TOML configuration. The default
configuration directory is &lt;code&gt;~/.config/totally&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-toml" data-lang="toml"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;[&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;prices&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;openai/gpt-5&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;]
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;input_per_million_usd&lt;/span&gt; = &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;1.25&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;cached_input_per_million_usd&lt;/span&gt; = &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;0.125&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;output_per_million_usd&lt;/span&gt; = &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;10.00&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;effective_from&lt;/span&gt; = &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;2025-08-07&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;source&lt;/span&gt; = &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;user&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Set &lt;code&gt;replace = true&lt;/code&gt; in an override to replace the model&amp;rsquo;s bundled price
history instead of adding an effective-date range.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Sessions</title><link>https://totally.sh/docs/sessions/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://totally.sh/docs/sessions/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Use &lt;code&gt;sessions&lt;/code&gt; to browse the agent sessions Totally has parsed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally sessions
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally sessions --since 7d
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally sessions --latest
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The default table includes each session&amp;rsquo;s identifier, working directory, model,
token use, estimated cost, and duration. Add &lt;code&gt;--full&lt;/code&gt; to avoid truncating table
values.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally sessions --full
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;For focused output, use one of these flags:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally sessions --ids
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally sessions --paths
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally sessions --summary
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally sessions --limit &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;20&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;--latest&lt;/code&gt; orders by most recently updated session and returns one result unless
you provide a different &lt;code&gt;--limit&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Show a session</title><link>https://totally.sh/docs/show/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://totally.sh/docs/show/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Use &lt;code&gt;show&lt;/code&gt; to inspect one session in detail. An unambiguous prefix of the
session ID is enough.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally show 019f44e4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;To inspect the most recently updated session instead, use &lt;code&gt;--latest&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally show --latest
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally show --latest --cwd .
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally show --latest --provider openai --model gpt-5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;--cwd&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;--provider&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;--model&lt;/code&gt; narrow &lt;code&gt;--latest&lt;/code&gt;; they are not used when
you provide a session ID directly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The report includes session metadata, transcript location, prompts, turns,
messages, tool calls, model and provider use, token breakdown, duration, and
estimated cost. Add &lt;code&gt;--full&lt;/code&gt; to keep long display values intact.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Stats</title><link>https://totally.sh/docs/stats/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://totally.sh/docs/stats/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Use &lt;code&gt;stats&lt;/code&gt; to aggregate session activity, token use, duration, and estimated
cost.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally stats --since 7d
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally stats --cwd . --since 30d
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally stats --provider openai --model gpt-5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Group results with one or more &lt;code&gt;--by&lt;/code&gt; flags:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally stats --since 30d --by cwd
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally stats --since 30d --by model
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;totally stats --since 30d --by day --by model
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Available group dimensions are &lt;code&gt;cwd&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;model&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;provider&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;day&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;week&lt;/code&gt;,
&lt;code&gt;month&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;session&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The default output is a terminal table. Select JSON explicitly for scripts.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>